s validated *empirically* only against confounded ground-truth pairs (S1/S3/S5), not asserted. All CAMUV results are contextualized as \"CAMUV (reconstruction)\".\n\n---\n\n## 2. Data generation (point 3 — full detail)\n\n**Generator.** Generic ANM engine: input ground-truth DAG over V = O ∪ L; each node j gets f_j (family + parameters, seed-drawn) and noise N_j. Sample X_j = f_j(Pa_j) + N_j in topological order.\n\n**Function families.** linear (a·x), sine (a·sin(b·x+φ)), quadratic (a·x²+b·x with centering), and cubic (a·x³ + b·x). Per edge, family drawn uniformly from the non-linear ones (linear only in dedicated ablation). Edge coefficients a ∈ {0.5, 1.0, 1.5}.\n\n**Noise.** Gaussian σ ∈ {0.1, 0.5, 1.0} (relative to signal scale), and Uniform(−u, u) with matching scale (in the uniform ablation).\n\n**Latent strength** (scale factor on all latent→observed edge coefficients): weak 0.3 / moderate 1.0 / strong 2.0.\n\n**Sample sizes** n ∈ {500, 2000, 10000}. **Repetitions**: 20–50 fixed seeds (e.g., seeds 0..49), identical seed stream across methods so all comparisons are paired.\n\n**Scenarios (ground-truth graphs over observed + latent nodes).**\n- **S1 — pure confounder (the core case):** 2 observed X, Y; 1 latent H with H→X, H→Y; no direct edge between X, Y.\n- **S2 — triangle (no latents):** X→Y, Y→Z, X→Z (3 observed) — sanity/control that the method still works with no latents.\n- **S3 — confounded chain:** X→Y→Z (3 observed) plus latent H→Y and H→Z (a hidden confounder in the chain head). Mixes direct edges (X→Y, Y→Z) with a confounded pair (Y,Z).\n- **S4 — direct edge + confounder on the same pair:** H→X, H→Y, and X→Y. Expected hard case for the pairwise rule (see §9, failure mode 1).\n- **S5 — scaling:** 4–6 observed + 1–2 latent; random DAG (Erdős–Rényi, bounded fan-in, ~1.5× expected edges) with a random latent confounder attached to 2–3 observed nodes. ~30 random graphs × seeds.\n\n**Data splits:** each generated dataset is used by every method (no indepe